<hr data-start="349" data-end="352" class="">
<h3 data-start="354" data-end="405" class="">üîß <strong data-start="361" data-end="405">Key Distillations from Deacon‚Äôs Argument</strong></h3>
<ol data-start="407" data-end="1714">
<li data-start="407" data-end="676" class="">
<p data-start="410" data-end="676" class=""><strong data-start="410" data-end="439">Decompression ‚â† Retrieval</strong><br data-start="439" data-end="442">
It‚Äôs not just unzipping a file. It‚Äôs an <strong data-start="485" data-end="525">emergent, constraint-based unfolding</strong> that depends on the context, substrate, and interactional rules. DNA isn‚Äôt meaningful alone‚Äîit‚Äôs <em data-start="623" data-end="675">meaningful within the body‚Äôs cellular architecture</em>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="678" data-end="901" class="">
<p data-start="681" data-end="901" class=""><strong data-start="681" data-end="716">We Mistake Noise for Complexity</strong><br data-start="716" data-end="719">
A frog smoothie is more entropic than a frog, but not more complex <em data-start="789" data-end="803">functionally</em>. The frog‚Äôs structured simplicity is born of a <strong data-start="851" data-end="900">compressed code + rich decompression scaffold</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="903" data-end="1227" class="">
<p data-start="906" data-end="1227" class=""><strong data-start="906" data-end="958">We Design for Compression, Not for Decompression</strong><br data-start="958" data-end="961">
Architecture assumes skilled labor and material. Blueprints work <em data-start="1029" data-end="1087">only because decompression is distributed into the world</em>. When that‚Äôs ignored‚Äîe.g., when AI summarizes or formats without modeling decompression‚Äîwe get <em data-start="1183" data-end="1199">semantic drift</em> and <em data-start="1204" data-end="1226">performative garbage</em>.</p>
