</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1124" data-end="1450" class="">
<p data-start="1127" data-end="1160" class=""><strong data-start="1127" data-end="1158">Sovereignty vs Situatedness</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1164" data-end="1450">
<li data-start="1164" data-end="1294" class="">
<p data-start="1166" data-end="1294" class=""><em data-start="1166" data-end="1172">Aley</em> introduces modal sovereignty as an anti-colonial design principle‚Äîinterfaces must let users define how meaning unfolds.</p>
