<hr data-start="240" data-end="243" class="">
<h2 data-start="245" data-end="314" class=""><strong data-start="248" data-end="314">Plenum Weaver as a Human-Centered Mixture of Experts Interface</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start="316" data-end="357" class=""><strong data-start="320" data-end="357">What is MoE (Mixture of Experts)?</strong></h3>
<p data-start="358" data-end="622" class="">In ML, a Mixture of Experts is an architecture where different submodels (experts) specialize in parts of the input space. A <strong data-start="483" data-end="503">gating mechanism</strong> routes inputs to the most appropriate experts dynamically, promoting <strong data-start="573" data-end="585">sparsity</strong>, <strong data-start="587" data-end="601">modularity</strong>, and <strong data-start="607" data-end="621">efficiency</strong>.</p>
