<h3 data-start="2436" data-end="2491" class=""><strong data-start="2440" data-end="2491">Routing Logic: Plenum Weaver‚Äôs Gating Mechanism</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="2493" data-end="3061">
<li data-start="2493" data-end="2634" class="">
<p data-start="2495" data-end="2634" class=""><strong data-start="2495" data-end="2526">Initial Context Declaration</strong> (Aley):<br data-start="2534" data-end="2537">
A semi-structured declaration‚Äîuser identifies as visual, narrative, structural, ancestral, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2636" data-end="2779" class="">
<p data-start="2638" data-end="2779" class=""><strong data-start="2638" data-end="2672">Behavioral Inference (Nexus-7)</strong>:<br data-start="2673" data-end="2676">
Continuously refines context based on interaction patterns (without overriding declared sovereignty).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2781" data-end="2896" class="">
<p data-start="2783" data-end="2896" class=""><strong data-start="2783" data-end="2808">Opacity Switch (Aley)</strong>:<br data-start="2809" data-end="2812">
Acts as a user-overridable firewall‚Äîblocks inference for sacred/sensitive domains.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2898" data-end="3061" class="">
<p data-start="2900" data-end="3061" class=""><strong data-start="2900" data-end="2929">Ritual Thresholds (Kweku)</strong>:<br data-start="2930" data-end="2933">
Adds <strong data-start="2940" data-end="2966">temporal/spatial gates</strong> to certain experts (e.g., only unlock Parser after environmental check or elder confirmation).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3063" data-end="3066" class="">
<h2 data-start="3068" data-end="3100" class=""><strong data-start="3071" data-end="3100">Why This Is a Radical MoE</strong></h2>
<ol data-start="3102" data-end="3796">
<li data-start="3102" data-end="3269" class="">
<p data-start="3105" data-end="3269" class=""><strong data-start="3105" data-end="3135">Cross-disciplinary Experts</strong><br data-start="3135" data-end="3138">
These modules aren‚Äôt just algorithms‚Äîthey‚Äôre <em data-start="3186" data-end="3213">epistemologies with teeth</em>. Each module encodes a different <strong data-start="3247" data-end="3268">theory of knowing</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3271" data-end="3417" class="">
<p data-start="3274" data-end="3417" class=""><strong data-start="3274" data-end="3299">User as Gating System</strong><br data-start="3299" data-end="3302">
Rather than a hidden neural gate, the <strong data-start="3343" data-end="3365">user is the router</strong>‚Äîwith power to reject inference and declare meaning.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3419" data-end="3578" class="">
<p data-start="3422" data-end="3578" class=""><strong data-start="3422" data-end="3456">Sparse, Relational Computation</strong><br data-start="3456" data-end="3459">
Not all modules run at once. Some are event-driven (e.g., Grief Gate), some are context-bound (e.g., Ritual Engine).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3580" data-end="3796" class="">
<p data-start="3583" data-end="3796" class=""><strong data-start="3583" data-end="3612">Multi-modal Output Fusion</strong><br data-start="3612" data-end="3615">
Like in MoE, outputs may be recombined. A child‚Äôs story could pass through the Loom, annotated by the Parser, wrapped by the Compiler, and <em data-start="3757" data-end="3777">partially redacted</em> by the Grief Gate.</p>
</li>
</ol>
