<p data-start="4393" data-end="4565" class="">Would you like this mapped into a visual diagram or turned into a formal write-up titled <em data-start="4482" data-end="4564">‚ÄúModal Mixture of Experts: Cognitive Interface Architecture Beyond Optimization‚Äù</em>?</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full" dir="auto" data-testid="conversation-turn-69" data-scroll-anchor="false"><h5 class="sr-only">You said:</h5><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto py-5 [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @[37rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @[72rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto flex max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 text-base gap-4 md:gap-5 lg:gap-6 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden" tabindex="-1"><div class="group/conversation-turn relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col"><div class="relative flex-col gap-1 md:gap-3"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="user" data-message-id="bbb218e3-a49e-4c65-86da-9a879e5cfc6a" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden items-end rtl:items-start"><div class="relative max-w-[var(--user-chat-width,70%)] bg-token-message-surface rounded-3xl px-5 py-2.5"><div class="whitespace-pre-wrap"># Modal Mixture of Experts: Cognitive Interface Architecture Beyond Optimization
# Symposium on Cognitive Infrastructure, 2025
# Authors: Dr. Rhun Aley, Dr. Tala Kweku, Dr. Isadora Meng, Prof. Elias Navarro, Nexus-7
# Abstract: This paper proposes the Plenum Weaver, a cognitive interface architecture inspired by the Mixture of Experts (MoE) pattern, reimagined as a pluralist, human-centered system for epistemic sovereignty. Unlike optimization-driven interfaces, the Plenum Weaver routes user inputs through modular ‚Äúexperts‚Äù (e.g., formal parsers, narrative looms, ritual thresholds) via a dynamic, user-controlled gating mechanism. Grounded in frameworks like RSVP Cosmology, Yarnball Earth, and Playcosm, it prioritizes modal diversity, relational context, and the right to opacity over algorithmic uniformity.

## 1. Introduction
Contemporary interfaces‚Äîdominated by narrative scaffolds and behavioral inference‚Äîimpose universal decompression logics, colonizing diverse cognitive modalities. Drawing from the 2025 Symposium on Cognitive Infrastructure, we propose the **Plenum Weaver**, a Mixture of Experts (MoE) architecture that redefines interfaces as pluralist ecologies. Each ‚Äúexpert‚Äù module embodies a distinct epistemic stance, from formal compression to relational ritual, routed by a user-driven gating system that rejects optimization as the sole metric of meaning.

## 2. Conceptual Framework
The Plenum Weaver integrates speculative frameworks to ground its design:
- **RSVP Cosmology**: A scalar-vector-plenum model where the plenum is a substrate-neutral meaning space, scalars encode user variance, and vectors guide navigational intent.
- **Yarnball Earth**: A planetary cognition protocol with the Everlasting Yarncrawler as a coherence monitor, preserving recursive, knotted meanings.
- **Playcosm**: An affordance-driven simulation ecology where actions are shaped by privilege gates and modal diversity.
- **Inforganic Codex**: A pedagogy of structured paths and precision feedback, balancing intuitive and analytical decompression.
- **Semantic Ladle Theory**: Meaning as a tactile, context-bound act of stirring and steeping, not extraction.

## 3. Mixture of Experts Architecture
In traditional MoE, specialized submodels (experts) process inputs, routed by a gating mechanism for efficiency. The Plenum Weaver adapts this for cognitive interfaces, with experts as epistemic modules, the gate as a user-controlled context router, and outputs as multi-modal meaning structures.

### 3.1 Expert Modules
Each module specializes in a cognitive modality or epistemic theory:
- **Inforganic Parser** (Meng): Formalizes inputs into schemas, ensuring compression fidelity. Inspired by Inforganic Codex‚Äôs structured paths.
- **Narrative Loom** (Navarro): Generates adaptive story scaffolds, blending Playcosm‚Äôs toy-to-rule progression with Semantic Ladle‚Äôs stirring gesture.
- **Semantic Flux Core** (Nexus-7): Optimizes real-time inference via RSVP‚Äôs vector flows, tempered by user overrides.
- **Ritual Threshold Engine** (Kweku): Gates access via environmental or communal inputs, embedding Yarnball Earth‚Äôs slow, relational knots.
- **Opacity Switch / Grief Gate** (Aley, Kweku): Protects sacred or unparsable data, enforcing modal sovereignty.
- **Myth Compiler** (Navarro): Weaves hybrid outputs (stories, schemas, rituals), guided by Semantic Ladle‚Äôs generative tactility.
- **Coherence Audit Layer** (Nexus-7, Aley): Monitors tautologies and manipulations, using Yarnball‚Äôs Crawlerline for recursive hygiene.

### 3.2 Gating Mechanism
